{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784648155,"nonce":"/l2IVYW+QfKHcUpyStYPd1cz404=","message":"## Root-cause analysis\n\nTwo things combine: `shazam` analyses more of the thread than `am` does, and\nthe mbox-path mismatch warning has no \"already applied\" filter — so it warns\nabout a trailer that is in fact already on the patch and will end up in the\ncommit regardless.\n\n**Why shazam warns but `am` doesn't.** `b4 shazam` force-enables the\nnewer-revision scan: `src/b4/mbox.py:1051` sets `cmdargs.checknewer = True`\nunconditionally, and line 1081 then calls `get_extra_series()`. `b4 am`\nleaves `checknewer` at its `--check-newer-revisions` default\n(`src/b4/command.py:68-69`, off), so it does not pull the extra\nrevision(s)/threads into the `LoreMailbox`. The additional messages shazam\ningests are what contribute the from/email-mismatched trailer (the\n`Suggested-by: Harry Yoo` carried on an older posting whose `From` is the\nzte.com.cn sender).\n\n**How the mismatch set is built.** A trailer is flagged as a mismatch when\nits identity doesn't match the `From` of the message it was found in —\n`LoreMessage.get_trailers()`, `src/b4/__init__.py:1795-1837` (email then\nname comparison; non-match → `mismatches`). Those are accumulated into\n`lser.trailer_mismatches` from follow-ups (`__init__.py:~438-442`) and from\nthe cross-revision `trailer_map` (`__init__.py:~506-509`) — the latter with\n**no dedup** against what's already on the patch.\n\n**The misleading part.** The warning is printed in `mbox.py:283-289`\nstraight from `lser.trailer_mismatches`, with no check that the trailer is\nalready present on the target patch. Contrast the ez.py path\n(`b4 trailers -u` / prep), which *does* suppress already-applied mismatches\nbefore warning — `src/b4/ez.py:1995-2000`:\n\n    if not cmdargs.sloppytrailers and mismatches:\n        for mismatch in list(mismatches):\n            if b4.LoreTrailer(name=mismatch[0], value=mismatch[1]) in parts[2]:\n                mismatches.remove(mismatch)\n\nThe mbox path has no equivalent. So when the v6 patch already carries the\n`Suggested-by:` line, `fix_trailers()`' own dedup keeps it from being\ndouble-added (correct end result — it lands in the commit), but the warning\nwas already emitted from the un-filtered mismatch set. The user is told a\ntrailer was \"ignored\" that was neither newly needed nor actually dropped.\n\n## Related bugs\n\nShares the trailer engine with `ddb36e5` (cross-revision trailer collection\nvia `trailer_map`) and `116ac85` (trailer parsing). This one is specifically\nthe missing already-applied filter on the mbox-path warning. No fix\nsuggestions per request.","files":null}]}